No iq or third-party MIT-labelled distance-function copy is distributed.

Platform adaptations use Android system fonts/EditText, caller-supplied Resources,
Context and per-session cache, main-thread dispatch, Android logging, Java Math.hypot
in place of ZXing's distance call, and primitive clamp/alpha helpers in place of
AndroidX calls. No ZXing or AndroidX code/artifact is bundled or linked. All actual
painting, text/entity geometry, compressed undo and GL readback remain upstream.
No third-party runtime Maven dependency is declared; Android platform APIs are the
runtime. Build-tool dependencies (Gradle/AGP) are not bundled in the application.
